{"id": "2026-07-25-news-saudi-led-coalition-strikes-hodeida-as-houthis-v", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Saudi-led coalition strikes Hodeida as Houthis vow response, widening the Gulf war", "summary": "A Saudi-led coalition struck the Houthi-held port of Hodeida on 24 July after Houthi attacks on Saudi tankers in the Red Sea; Houthis vowed to retaliate on 25 July.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-houthis-vow-response-to-dangerous-escalation-by-saudi-arabia/live-78107211", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["disputed"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "A Saudi-led coalition struck the Houthi-held Yemeni port of Hodeida on Friday 24 July, and the Iran-backed Houthis vowed to retaliate on Saturday 25 July, pulling Saudi Arabia directly into the widening Gulf war. The strikes followed several days of Houthi attacks on Saudi oil tankers in the Red Sea; Riyadh said it hit military targets and would \"do everything necessary\" to protect its shipping against a Houthi-enforced maritime blockade, while the Houthis said the strikes hit civilian infrastructure in Hodeida and injured two people. The flare-up opens a new front alongside the ongoing US-Iran confrontation over the Strait of Hormuz, and the UN warned on 24 July against a wider escalation as fighting intensified around the Red Sea, a corridor that normally carries a large share of world seaborne trade.", "why": "A direct Saudi-Houthi exchange layered on top of the US-Iran war threatens both of the region's two critical maritime chokepoints (Hormuz and Bab al-Mandeb) at once, and any sustained closure of Red Sea shipping feeds straight into global energy and freight costs.", "thread_id": "2026-07-25-news-saudi-led-coalition-strikes-hodeida-as-houthis-v", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-25", "event_date": "2026-07-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Saudi Arabia", "Houthis", "Yemen", "Hodeida", "Red Sea", "Iran", "Bab al-Mandeb"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-europe-wildfires-force-200-000-from-homes-across", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Europe wildfires force 200,000 from homes across France, Spain and Italy", "summary": "Wildfires in western France, central Spain and Italy have forced roughly 200,000 people to evacuate amid a heatwave, with national emergencies declared.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/europe-wildfires-rage-on-forcing-200-000-from-homes/a-78109406", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Wildfires across western France, central Spain and Italy have now forced roughly 200,000 people from their homes, authorities said Saturday 25 July, as separate blazes merged and hot, dry, windy conditions kept them out of control. In France's Gironde and Landes departments the fire drove mass evacuations around Bordeaux, while Spain - which declared its first-ever national wildfire emergency on Thursday 23 July over blazes near Madrid and in Avila - and Italy continued to battle major fires amid a Europe-wide heatwave. DW reported conditions that made it \"nearly impossible for firefighters to gain the upper hand.\"", "why": "The evacuation total has roughly quadrupled in two days, marking one of the worst fire seasons on record for southern Europe and straining cross-border firefighting resources at peak summer.", "thread_id": "2026-07-23-news-wildfires-kill-three-firefighters-across-france", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-23", "event_date": "2026-07-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "Spain", "Italy", "Gironde", "Bordeaux", "Madrid"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-poland-s-opposition-pis-splits-as-kaczynski-move", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Poland's opposition PiS splits as Kaczynski moves against Morawiecki", "summary": "PiS leader Jaroslaw Kaczynski said on 24 July that more than 30 delegates had forfeited membership in a power struggle centred on former PM Mateusz Morawiecki.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/poland-s-main-opposition-collapses-over-far-right-slide/a-78106475", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Poland's main opposition party, the national-conservative Law and Justice (PiS), split on Friday 24 July as leader Jaroslaw Kaczynski said more than 30 of the party's parliamentary delegates had \"effectively forfeited their membership\" in a power struggle centred on former Prime Minister Mateusz Morawiecki. Kaczynski accused Morawiecki of splitting the party; DW framed the move - tied to PiS's drift toward the far right - as one that could sharply weaken the party's popularity.", "why": "PiS is the principal opposition to Poland's governing centrist coalition, and a fracture on the right reshapes the electoral map of the EU's fifth-largest member state ahead of future national contests.", "thread_id": "2026-07-25-news-poland-s-opposition-pis-splits-as-kaczynski-move", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-25", "event_date": "2026-07-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Poland", "Law and Justice", "Jaroslaw Kaczynski", "Mateusz Morawiecki"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-india-s-education-minister-dharmendra-pradhan-re", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "India's education minister Dharmendra Pradhan resigns amid youth protests", "summary": "Education Minister Dharmendra Pradhan announced his resignation on 25 July amid a 36-day youth-led protest movement at Jantar Mantar in New Delhi.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-education-minister-dharmendra-pradhan-announces-resignation-amid-growing-protests/live-78108089", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "India's education minister, Dharmendra Pradhan, announced his resignation on Saturday 25 July amid a youth-led protest movement that has occupied the Jantar Mantar grounds in New Delhi for 36 days. Pradhan's departure is the first cabinet-level concession to the \"Cockroach\" movement (the youth-led Cockroach Janta Party), with a second round of talks between the movement and the government scheduled and police tightening security as crowds are expected to swell over the weekend.", "why": "A sitting minister stepping down over sustained street protest is a rare retreat for Prime Minister Narendra Modi's government and a test of whether the youth movement can convert pressure into policy change.", "thread_id": "2026-07-25-news-india-s-education-minister-dharmendra-pradhan-re", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-25", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["India", "Dharmendra Pradhan", "Narendra Modi", "New Delhi", "Cockroach Janta Party"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-un-reappoints-volker-turk-as-human-rights-chief", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "UN reappoints Volker Turk as human rights chief for four more years", "summary": "The UN General Assembly voted 144-10 on 24 July to reappoint Volker Turk as High Commissioner for Human Rights, whose office is based in Geneva.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/international/uno-hochkommissar-volker-tuerk-fuer-weitere-vier-jahre-im-amt", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The UN General Assembly voted 144 to 10 on Friday 24 July to reappoint Volker Turk as UN High Commissioner for Human Rights for a second four-year term, keeping the Geneva-based office in the hands of a diplomat who has repeatedly and sharply criticised both Russia's war in Ukraine and Israel's conduct in Gaza. The vote followed a debate with pointed criticism of the Austrian: Israel's representative accused Turk of lacking \"professionalism and leadership\" and of bias.", "why": "The OHCHR is one of International Geneva's flagship institutions, and a strong endorsement re-anchors an outspoken human-rights mandate in the city even as the office draws fire from governments it scrutinises.", "thread_id": "2026-07-25-news-un-reappoints-volker-turk-as-human-rights-chief", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-25", "event_date": "2026-07-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Volker Turk", "OHCHR", "United Nations", "Geneva"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-russian-embassy-in-bern-issues-communique-critic", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian embassy in Bern issues communique criticising Switzerland's human rights record", "summary": "Russia's embassy in Bern published a communique calling Switzerland's model-country status on human rights compromised, about two months before the neutrality-initiative vote.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/des-carences-graves-la-russie-fait-la-lecon-a-la-suisse-sur-le-respect-des-droits-de-l-homme", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "geopolitics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Russia's embassy in Bern published a caustic communique claiming Switzerland's own human-rights record shows \"serious deficiencies\" and that its standing as a model country is \"compromised,\" Le Temps reported. The statement - Moscow effectively lecturing Bern on rights - landed roughly two months before Switzerland's popular vote on the neutrality initiative, a context Le Temps flagged as pointed given the sharp Russia-Switzerland friction since the war in Ukraine.", "why": "It is a piece of diplomatic pressure aimed at Swiss domestic debate, using human-rights framing to needle a country Moscow accuses of abandoning neutrality.", "thread_id": "2026-07-25-news-russian-embassy-in-bern-issues-communique-critic", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-25", "event_date": "2026-07-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Switzerland", "Bern", "neutrality initiative"]}
{"id": "2026-07-25-news-swiss-cantons-impose-fireworks-bans-for-1-august", "date": "2026-07-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss cantons impose fireworks bans for 1 August amid drought", "summary": "A growing number of Swiss cantons have banned private fireworks for the 1 August national holiday because of wildfire risk from prolonged drought.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/stiller-nationalfeiertag-kantone-erlassen-feuerwerksverbote-fuer-1-august-die-uebersicht", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A growing number of Swiss cantons have banned private fireworks for the 1 August national holiday, SRF reported Saturday 25 July, so that this year's Bundesfeier will be unusually quiet. With an absolute open-air fire ban or a forest-and-forest-edge fire ban already in force across most of the country for weeks amid an entrenched drought and heatwave, cantons are extending the restrictions to holiday fireworks to avoid sparking wildfires; some municipalities have gone further.", "why": "It is a concrete, daily-life consequence of the drought reaching into a national tradition, and a signal of how deep the wildfire risk now runs across Switzerland.", "thread_id": "2026-07-02-news-heatwave-absolute-fire-bans-imposed-in-valais-an", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-02", "event_date": "2026-07-02", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Bundesfeier"]}
